<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{% if draft_as_of %}DRAFT · {% endif %}{{ overall.report_period_label }} — PS-0 Market Report</title><meta name="author" content="Isaac Akinmokun"><meta name="description" content="{{ social_description }}"><link rel="canonical" href="https://reports.akinmokun.com/{{ report_key }}/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico"><meta name="robots" content="{{ 'noindex, nofollow' if preview else 'index, follow' }}"><meta property="og:title" content="{{ overall.report_period_label }} — PS-0 Market Report"><meta property="og:description" content="{{ social_description }}"><meta property="og:url" content="https://reports.akinmokun.com/{{ report_key }}/"><meta property="og:type" content="article"><meta property="og:image" content="https://reports.akinmokun.com/social-card.png"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><script type="application/ld+json">{{ article_schema | tojson }}</script><style>{{ embedded_fonts_css | safe }}{% include 'partials/site.css' %}
.report{--report-paper:#fffefa;--report-ink:#222c25;--report-muted:#5d685f;--report-line:#dfdfd5;--report-accent:#74491c;--report-secondary:#39483d;--report-subtle:#f4f2eb;--report-rule:#aaa99a;--report-track:#efede6;--report-bar:#42664e;}
.report{max-width:960px;margin:auto;padding:0 30px 60px;background:var(--report-paper);color:var(--report-ink);font:18px/1.6 'New Computer Modern',Georgia,serif}.report h1,.report h2,.report h3{font-family:'New Computer Modern',Georgia,serif}.report h1{font-size:clamp(38px,5vw,64px);line-height:1.05;font-weight:400}.report h2{font-size:32px;font-weight:400;margin:10px 0 20px}.report h3{font-size:21px;margin:20px 0 8px}.report p{max-width:80ch}.report .muted{color:var(--report-muted)}.report .eyebrow{color:var(--report-accent)}.report-page{padding:45px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--report-line)}.cover{padding:70px 0 50px}.cover-rule{width:70px;height:4px;background:#8a5b25;margin:35px 0}.cover-deck{font-size:23px;max-width:32em}.facts{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:35px;margin:35px 0;font:12px/1.7 Merriweather,Georgia,serif}.facts strong{display:block;font-size:22px;font-weight:400}.kpis{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;border-block:1px solid var(--report-line);padding:18px 0;margin:25px 0}.kpis span{display:block;font:10px/1.5 Merriweather,Georgia,serif;color:var(--report-muted)}.kpis strong{font-size:28px;font-weight:400}figure{margin:25px 0;break-inside:avoid}figure svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:320px}figcaption{font:11px/1.7 Merriweather,Georgia,serif;color:var(--report-muted);border-top:1px solid var(--report-line);padding-top:10px}.figure-heading{font-size:20px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:12px}.takeaways{padding-left:23px}.takeaways li{margin:12px 0}.note{font:12px/1.7 Merriweather,Georgia,serif;border-left:2px solid #8a5b25;padding:10px 18px;margin:25px 0}.report table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font:12px/1.5 Merriweather,Georgia,serif}.report th,.report td{text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--report-line);padding:9px 6px}.report th{font-size:10px;color:var(--report-muted)}.report td:last-child{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.toc{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;font:11px Merriweather,Georgia,serif;margin:25px 0}.appendix{margin:30px 0;font-size:14px}.appendix summary{cursor:pointer}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto}.preview-banner{background:#f2e9d9;color:#5d3a16;padding:12px;text-align:center;font:12px Merriweather,serif}.methodology p{font-size:15px}.report .button{font-family:Merriweather,Georgia,serif;color:var(--report-ink);border-color:var(--report-rule)}.report .button.primary{background:var(--report-ink);color:var(--report-paper)}.running-title{font:10px Merriweather,serif;color:var(--report-muted)}
@page{size:A4;margin:18mm 18mm 20mm;@bottom-left{content:'PS-0 / MARKET RESEARCH';font:8pt sans-serif;color:var(--report-muted)}@bottom-right{content:counter(page);font:8pt sans-serif;color:var(--report-muted)}}
@media print{html,body{background:white!important;color:var(--report-ink)!important}.shell{max-width:none;padding:0}.site-header,.site-footer,.toc,.actions,.appendix,.preview-banner{display:none!important}.report{padding:0;max-width:none;background:white;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.48}.report-page{break-before:page;padding:0;border:0}.cover{break-before:auto;padding-top:22mm;min-height:235mm}.report h1{font-size:40pt}.report h2{font-size:25pt}.report h3{font-size:16pt}.report p{orphans:3;widows:3}h2,h3{break-after:avoid}figure{margin:15px 0}figure svg{max-height:75mm}.kpis{margin:15px 0;padding:12px 0}.kpis strong{font-size:20pt}.report .table-scroll{overflow:visible}.report table{font-size:7.5pt}.report thead{display:table-header-group}.report tr{break-inside:avoid;page-break-inside:avoid}.report td,.report th{padding:4px}.facts{display:table;width:100%;table-layout:fixed;font-size:9pt}.facts>div{display:table-cell;width:33.333%;padding-right:18px;vertical-align:top}.methodology p{font-size:10pt}.note{font-size:9pt}a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}}
@media(max-width:650px){.report{padding-inline:20px;font-size:17px}.kpis{gap:12px}.kpis strong{font-size:24px}.report table{font-size:11px}.facts{gap:20px}.report-page{padding-block:30px}}

@media screen{:root[data-theme=dark] .report{--report-paper:#000;--report-ink:#f0f0f0;--report-muted:#a3a3ab;--report-line:#303034;--report-accent:#e5c38b;--report-secondary:#c5c5cc;--report-subtle:#111;--report-rule:#52525b;color-scheme:dark}:root[data-theme=dark] .report figure svg{background:#fffefa;padding:12px;border-radius:2px}}
</style><script>{% include 'partials/theme.js' %}</script></head><body><div class="shell">{% include 'partials/header.html.j2' %}</div>{% if preview %}<div class="preview-banner">{% if draft_as_of %}DRAFT — {{ overall.report_period_label }} to date · Snapshot exported {{ draft_as_of }} · Unfinished month; not published{% else %}Future issue structure study · Uses {{ overall.report_period_label }} data from the issue published {{ published_date }} · This is not a new issue.{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}<main id="main-content" class="report"><section class="cover report-page"><span class="eyebrow">PS-0 / Market research · {% if draft_as_of %}Unpublished draft{% else %}Issue {{ issue_number }}{% endif %}</span><div class="cover-rule"></div><h1>Nigerian property.<br>A closer reading.</h1><p class="cover-deck">{{ overall.report_period_label }}<br>Observed inventory, advertised asking prices, and price adjustments.</p><div class="facts"><div><strong>{{ overall.num_cities }}</strong>Cities observed</div><div><strong>{{ overall.unique_neighbourhoods }}</strong>City / neighbourhood pairs</div><div><strong>{{ overall.num_weeks }}</strong>Weeks represented</div></div><p class="running-title">Research by Isaac Akinmokun · {% if draft_as_of %}Draft as of {{ draft_as_of }} — not published{% if draft_source_last_seen %}<br>Latest source observation: {{ draft_source_last_seen }}. Export date is not a new observation date.{% endif %}{% else %}Published {{ published_date }}{% endif %}<br>Snapshot starts: {{ overall.date_range.start }} to {{ overall.date_range.end }}</p><div class="actions">{% if has_pdf %}<a class="button primary" href="{{ pdf_filename }}" download>Download PDF ↓</a>{% endif %}<a class="button" href="#brief">Read the findings →</a></div><nav class="toc" aria-label="Report contents"><a href="#brief">Brief</a>{% for market in publication %}<a href="#{{ market }}">{{ market|title }}</a>{% endfor %}<a href="#methodology">Methodology</a><a href="#appendix">Detailed tables</a></nav></section>
<section id="brief" class="report-page"><span class="eyebrow">01 / The brief</span><h2>The period at a glance.</h2>{% if metrics.quality %}<div class="note">{% if draft_as_of %}Month-to-date draft as of {{ draft_as_of }}. {% if draft_source_last_seen %}Latest source observation: {{ draft_source_last_seen }}. Reconstructed inventory after this date does not imply a fresh scrape. {% endif %}{% if metrics.quality.partial_week_starts %}Incomplete current week: {{ metrics.quality.partial_week_starts|join(", ") }}. Its counts must not be compared with full weeks as evidence of a decline. {% endif %}{% endif %}Coverage: {{ metrics.quality.included_week_starts|length }} of {{ metrics.quality.expected_week_starts|length }} calendar week starts represented. {% if metrics.quality.missing_week_starts %}Missing source weeks: {{ metrics.quality.missing_week_starts|join(', ') }}. {% endif %}{% if metrics.quality.excluded_week_starts %}Excluded by the trailing-volume heuristic: {{ metrics.quality.excluded_week_starts|join(', ') }}. {% endif %}{{ metrics.quality.missing_price_rows }} of {{ metrics.quality.snapshot_rows }} source groups have no usable median price, including {{ metrics.quality.invalid_price_rows }} with non-positive or non-finite values. These groups remain in inventory totals.</div>{% endif %}<p>Evidence from the advertised properties observed by PS-0. Sales and rentals are read separately, with comparisons grounded in the property classes and locations represented.</p>{% for market in publication %}{% set data=metrics[market] %}<h3>{{ market|title }}</h3><div class="kpis"><div><strong>{{ '{:,}'.format(data.overall.peak_active_listings) }}</strong><span>Peak active · highest weekly total</span></div><div><strong>{{ '{:,}'.format(data.overall.total_new_listings) }}</strong><span>First discovered this period</span></div><div><strong>{{ '{:,}'.format(data.overall.total_price_reductions) }}</strong><span>Price reduction events</span></div></div><ul class="takeaways">{% for point in narrative[market].key_takeaways[:3] %}<li>{{ point }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endfor %}<div class="note">These are advertised asking prices and observed listing counts. They do not measure completed transactions or represent every property in Nigeria. Historical pricing is reconstructed from current records; this report does not infer historical price appreciation.</div></section>
{% for market, content in publication.items() %}{% set data=metrics[market] %}{% set text=narrative[market] %}{% set rent=market=='rentals' %}
<section id="{{ market }}" class="report-page"><span class="eyebrow">{{ '02' if market=='sales' else '03' }} / {{ market }} · Inventory</span><h2>{{ 'Sales Market Analysis' if market=='sales' else 'Rentals Market Analysis' }}</h2>{% for paragraph in text.inventory_narrative.split('\n\n') %}<p>{{ paragraph }}</p>{% endfor %}<figure><div class="figure-heading">Observed inventory through the period</div>{{ content.figures.inventory|safe }}<figcaption>Weekly active listings, grouped by snapshot start date. A listing may appear in multiple weeks. Changes can reflect observation coverage as well as supply.</figcaption></figure><figure><div class="figure-heading">The property mix</div>{{ content.figures.composition|safe }}<figcaption>Average weekly active inventory, using the market's included week count as the denominator. Six largest classes shown; remaining classes are combined. Displayed counts are rounded.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="report-page"><span class="eyebrow">{{ market }} / Asking prices</span><h2>Compare like with like.</h2><p>{{ text.pricing_narrative }}</p><figure><div class="figure-heading">Class-specific area benchmarks {{ '(NGN / year)' if rent else '(NGN)' }}</div>{{ content.figures.pricing|safe }}<figcaption>Independent horizontal scales for each property class. Green: first eligible affordable area. Amber: first eligible expensive area. Points use means of observed area group medians, not a listing-level distribution. Area names and figures appear below.</figcaption></figure><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Property class / benchmark</th><th>Area</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Mean group median{{ ' / yr' if rent else '' }}</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in content.pricing %}<tr><td>{{ row.property_class }}<br><small>{{ row.tier }}</small></td><td>{{ row.neighbourhood }}<br><small>{{ row.city|title }}</small></td><td>{{ row.num_price_weeks_observed|default(row.num_weeks_observed) }} priced / {{ data.overall.num_weeks }} report weeks<br>{{ row.avg_weekly_active_listings|default('N/A') }} active / observed week</td><td>{{ row.avg_median_price_ngn|money }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="report-page"><span class="eyebrow">{{ market }} / Price adjustments</span><h2>Where expectations shift.</h2><p>{{ text.price_reduction_narrative }}</p><figure><div class="figure-heading">Recorded reductions by city</div>{{ content.figures.reductions|safe }}<figcaption>Event counts for the six cities with the most reductions. Multiple reductions on one listing count separately. Larger markets can generate more events; these are counts, not reduction rates.</figcaption></figure><div class="note"><strong>{{ '{:,}'.format(data.price_reduction_analysis.total_price_reductions) }} events</strong> observed. Peak week: {{ data.price_reduction_analysis.peak_week or 'not available' }} ({{ data.price_reduction_analysis.peak_week_count }} events). The data records adjustments to asking prices; it does not establish the final negotiated price.</div><h3>Reading the evidence</h3><p>Inventory, property mix and asking-price benchmarks should be considered together. Coverage and class composition can move aggregate figures even when comparable properties have not changed price. See the detailed tables for the observations behind these figures.</p></section>
{% endfor %}
<section class="report-page methodology" id="methodology"><span class="eyebrow">Research notes</span><h2>How to read this report.</h2><p><strong>Source and scope.</strong> PS-0 reconstructs weekly groups from listing records and price-change history. Each group identifies city, neighbourhood, week, property class and market type. Sales and rentals are separate; short lets are excluded. Residential, land and commercial classes may be represented.</p><p><strong>Inventory.</strong> Peak is the highest weekly total. Cumulative counts measure listing-weeks. The period includes weeks whose start date falls inside its calendar window; a final week can extend beyond month-end. The final week is excluded when its inventory falls below 30% of the preceding weeks' median, a heuristic that may also remove a real decline.</p><p><strong>Pricing.</strong> Group prices are medians. Area benchmarks average those observed group medians; aggregate prices are unweighted medians of group medians. Affordable and expensive rankings require average observed weekly inventory of at least three and five listings respectively. Amounts are stored in kobo and divided by 100 for NGN display. Rental amounts assume annual asking rents in the source.</p><p><strong>Historical limitations.</strong> Current listing status, price and property classification are reused in reconstructed weeks. These are not immutable historical price observations. Missing observations and portal access can influence coverage; the pipeline does not explicitly annotate outages.</p><p><strong>Days on market.</strong> DOM measures first observation to the earlier of last observation and the week's end, with a one-day floor. Discovery can occur after the actual listing date. It is omitted from the main comparisons because this limitation constrains interpretation.</p><p><strong>Authorship and use.</strong> Research by Isaac Akinmokun, with automated narrative assistance. Figures and tables derive from the computed inputs. This publication supplies general market observations, not investment advice. Source coverage and asking prices should be independently assessed before decisions.</p><p class="running-title">PS-0 Market Reports · {{ overall.report_period_label }} · reports.akinmokun.com</p></section>
<details class="appendix" id="appendix"><summary>Detailed evidence tables — expand the appendix</summary><p>The PDF contains the core publication. These additional tables are available in the HTML edition.</p>{% for market, content in publication.items() %}<h2>{{ market|title }} / Class tables</h2>{% for name, data in content.classes %}<h3>{{ name|replace('_',' ')|title }}</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Week start</th><th>Active</th><th>New</th><th>Reductions</th><th>Median of group medians</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in data.weekly_aggregates %}<tr><td>{{ row.week }}</td><td>{{ row.active_listing_count }}</td><td>{{ row.new_listings_count }}</td><td>{{ row.price_reduced_count }}</td><td>{{ row.median_price_ngn|money }}{{ ' / yr' if market=='rentals' else '' }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}</details></main><div class="shell">{% include 'partials/footer.html.j2' %}</div></body></html>
